Build prerequistes:
  - Gecko SDK for your compiler/platform
  - Pidgin source tree (for headers)
  - libpurple.so (must have been built from the pidgin source tree)
  - GTK devel packages (needed to build Pidgin, so you should have it anyway)

To compile this, use configure with the relevant paths:

 ./configure --with-gecko=/path/to/gecko/sdk --with-gtk=/path/to/gtk-dev
   --with-pidgin-src=/path/to/pidgin/src/tree --with-libpurple=/path/to/libpurple.so
 make
 make install

The application will be installed in ../testapp/

By default on Windows this attempts to build using MSVC.  If you want to use
mingw to compile instead:

 CC=gcc CXX=g++ LD=g++ ./configure ...

Note that this means you need to use a mingw-built Gecko SDK, since mingw-gcc
does not like the MSVC-built Gecko SDK distributed by mozilla.com
